     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Hi,</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt\"><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span>I am new to cameratrapR and R in general. I am trying to create a recordTable, but the column labeled &quot;metadata_SiteID&quot; shows &quot;NA&quot; for all entries. The other metadata columns (metadata_Number, metadata_Species, metadata_Sex, etc.) appear to be correct on the recordTable. I believe the issue might be the stationCol function as I am not sure if stationCol should be set to HierarchicalSubject or not. <u></u><u></u></span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Example of my hierarchical subject column: Age_class|Juvenile, Group|Bird, Number|1, Sex|Male, Species|Elliot&#39;s Pheasant, Site ID|C44<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:mediu